# Token-ops inventory — authoritative list of every ERC20 token-moving call
# site in production `src/`. Every new `transfer` / `transferFrom` /
# `safeTransfer` / `safeTransferFrom` call, and every Permit2 pull
# (`permitTransferFrom` / `permitWitnessTransferFrom`), merged into `src/` must be added
# here, keyed to the function that makes it, with the spec rule that upholds
# its invariant, or the lint-token-ops.sh gate will refuse the merge.
#
# Format: `<path> :: <Contract>.<function> :: <call> | <role> | <spec coverage>`
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# `<call>` is the call's text with whitespace collapsed, as the source writes
# it (`token.safeTransferFrom(from, address(this), amount)`). When one function
# makes the same call twice, the second and later carry ` #2`, ` #3` after the
# call, in source order. No line number: an edit that moves lines leaves this
# file current; a call added, deleted, rewritten or moved to another function
# does not.
#
# Spec coverage column lists the CVL rule(s) in certora/TokenOpsVerification.spec
# (or a sister spec) that prove the call's invariant. Pending entries are
# marked `[PENDING: <spec target>]` — new entries MAY ship pending, but must
# be followed by a spec PR within the same sprint.

src/core/kernel/FigaroCore.sol :: FigaroCore._pullExact :: token.safeTransferFrom(from, address(this), amount) | commit bond pull | commitBuyerExactDelta, commitSellerExactDelta, commitContractExactDelta, commitAllowanceDrainSafety, commitTokenConservation
src/core/kernel/FigaroCore.sol :: FigaroCore.resolveProcess :: currency.safeTransfer(c.seller, sellerPayout) | seller payout | resolveSingleOrderPayout, resolveSingleOrderConservation
src/core/kernel/FigaroCore.sol :: FigaroCore.resolveProcess :: currency.safeTransfer(buyer, buyerPayout) | buyer payout | resolveSingleOrderPayout, resolveSingleOrderConservation

# WitnessSwapAndCommitCoordinator — the swap-and-commit coordinator (its unhardened
# predecessor, which left the swap route outside every signature, was deleted before
# any deployment — git history). TRACKED here: the swap route is bound into a
# Permit2 witness, so its token movements are an accounted surface. Deploy-wired and
# UI-wired (the checkout's swap-funding panel builds the witness-signed buyer leg —
# docs/CONTRACTS.md owns the wiring). The Permit2 pull moves the party's input token into the
# coordinator under the party's witness signature; the two transfers forward
# swapped bond currency / unconsumed input to the party (`c.buyer`/`c.seller`);
# none of the three touches FigaroCore escrow (FigaroCore pulls the bond itself).
# certora/SwapCoordinatorTokenOps.spec's coordinatorTokenConservation proves that on every
# completing swapAndCommit the coordinator ends holding none of either token (the
# `SlippageResidualStaysWithParty` / `InputResidualRefunded` Foundry tests assert the same).
src/app/WitnessSwapAndCommitCoordinator.sol :: WitnessSwapAndCommitCoordinator._fund :: permit2.permitWitnessTransferFrom(IPermit2WitnessTransfer.PermitTransferFrom({ permitted: IPermit2WitnessTransfer.TokenPermissions({token: f.inputToken, amount: f.maxInput}), nonce: f.permitNonce, deadline: f.permitDeadline }), IPermit2WitnessTransfer.SignatureTransferDetails({to: address(this), requestedAmount: f.maxInput}), party, witness, WITNESS_TYPE_STRING, f.permitSignature) | party input token → coordinator (Permit2 witness pull, route bound in the signed digest) | coordinatorTokenConservation (certora/SwapCoordinatorTokenOps.spec)
src/app/WitnessSwapAndCommitCoordinator.sol :: WitnessSwapAndCommitCoordinator._fund :: IERC20(bondCurrency).safeTransfer(party, received) | bond currency → party | coordinatorTokenConservation (certora/SwapCoordinatorTokenOps.spec)
src/app/WitnessSwapAndCommitCoordinator.sol :: WitnessSwapAndCommitCoordinator._fund :: IERC20(f.inputToken).safeTransfer(party, inputResidual) | input residual refund → party | coordinatorTokenConservation (certora/SwapCoordinatorTokenOps.spec)

# FigaroBatchVerifier — the batch-settlement verifier (proof-apparatus
# rebuild, witness model). BatchVerifierTokenOps.spec covers both sites:
# single-position rules with the documented inductive generalization;
# registered summarized as a revert-only view (sound — the anchor gate
# refuses settlement, never moves a token). Cloud run green 2026-07-16.
src/core/verifier/FigaroBatchVerifier.sol :: FigaroBatchVerifier._executePositions :: IERC20(p.token).safeTransfer(p.user, net) | net payout → user | singlePositionUserDelta, singlePositionContractDelta, singlePositionAllowanceDrainSafety, singlePositionConservation
src/core/verifier/FigaroBatchVerifier.sol :: FigaroBatchVerifier._pullExact :: token.safeTransferFrom(from, address(this), amount) | net deposit pull | singlePositionUserDelta, singlePositionContractDelta, singlePositionAllowanceDrainSafety, singlePositionConservation
